Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the three reactive NPC layers (API in-transaction hedge/dominance, npc-worker
bursts, legacy simulator servo) with one engine driven entirely by admin settings:

* shared/npc-organic: versioned settings document + field schema (labels, ranges,
  applies live/next round/settlement), organic plan maths (trickle-in, Poisson
  arrivals, tiers, lead target, FOMO), directive settlement (net positions, zero-profit
  cap, surplus to real winners, ghost town), final-injection planner (Lightning
  Dilution by bisection, Ghost Town), Redis keys and a cached engine-mode reader.
* engine/npc-organic: OrganicNpcEngine (round sessions, projection + steering every
  5 s, lock at T − lead with grace key, sliced whale injection), settings source
  (push + poll + DB fallback), exposure reader, audit store, host wiring and a live
  organic/legacy switch; directive settlement applier wired into
  BattleSettlementService; snapshot carries trader_count + locked.
* api: ROUND_LOCKED (409) in fast validation, full validation and inside the trade
  transaction; legacy hedge/dominance paths skipped in organic mode; admin endpoints
  /admin/npc/organic/{schema,settings,mode,status,live,rounds}; battleLocked forwarded
  to the battle room.
* npc-worker: hosts the engine, routes real trades / battle events to it, ignores
  reactive bursts and align-at-close in organic mode.
* prisma: npc_round_audit table (plan, timeline, projection, final injection,
  settlement invariants) + migration.

Tests: shared npc-organic specs (27), engine organic-npc-engine spec (8), typecheck of
api / engine / npc-worker; workbench browser smoke with one real trader (lock, LOCKED
buttons, ROUND_LOCKED, invariants, admin form round-trip).

