index 0000000..bb1c551
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/NPC-ORGANIC-ENGINE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# Organic NPC Engine
+
+Implements the *TickTrade Master NPC Architecture and Risk Management Directives 2.1* and the
+*Live Testing & Artificial Reaction Flaw* memo. It replaces the three reactive layers that used to
+mirror every real order (API in-transaction hedge/dominance, npc-worker reactive bursts, legacy
+simulator servo) with one engine whose every input is an admin setting.
+
+## What runs where
+
+| Process | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `npc-worker` (default, `NPC_WORKER_ENABLED=1`) or `engine` (`NPC_SIM_IN_ENGINE`) | Hosts the engine (`apps/engine/src/npc-organic/`). One leader trades; START/STOP from the admin page go through `NpcEngineSwitch`, which runs exactly one of *organic* / *legacy*. |
+| `api` | Saves settings (`PUT /admin/npc/organic/settings`), mirrors them to Redis, pushes them on `engine:events:npc.organic.settings`; rejects orders after the lock (`ROUND_LOCKED`, HTTP 409); skips the legacy hedge / dominance paths while the mode is `organic`; forwards `battleLocked` to the battle room. |
+| `settlement-worker` / `engine` | `BattleSettlementService` uses the directive settlement (`applyDirectiveSettlement`) for rounds the organic engine handled and writes the audit row `npc_round_audit`. |
+
+Mode is stored in `system_settings.npc_engine_mode` (`organic` default, `legacy` fallback) and mirrored to
+Redis `ticktrade:npc:engine_mode`. Switching is live: the running engine stops and the other one starts.
+
+## Round flow (organic mode)
+
+1. **Round start** — no NPC trades at 0 ms. `initialSpawnsMin..Max` NPCs are drawn (more during peak hours)
+   and enter after `spawnDelayMinMs..MaxMs`. A lead side and lead share (`asymmetry.leadSharePct*`) are drawn
+   for the round; the lead side stays ahead for `organicWindowFraction` of the round. No parity servo.
+2. **Momentum** — arrivals follow a Poisson process whose rate ramps from `baseArrivalsPerMinute` to
+   `peakArrivalsPerMinute` (`rampToPeakFraction`), fades after `lateFadeFraction`, is multiplied during peak
+   hours and for `realTradeBoostSeconds` after a real trade (`realTradeBoostMultiplier`). Quiet periods
+   (`quietPeriodChancePct`) pause the flow. `maxDistinctNpcsPerRound` / `maxSimVolumePerRound` cap the round.
+3. **Tiers** — the roster is split into whale / mid / retail by `rosterSharePct`; each trade picks a tier by
+   `tradeSharePct` and a stake in `[stakeMin, stakeMax]` (jitter, human-looking ladder rounding).
+4. **Defense A (steering)** — every 5 s the engine projects the settlement; when real winners would be paid
+   more than the net real loser pool, `steeringStrengthPct` of the organic orders are placed on the side that
+   lowers the exposure (from `steeringStartFraction` of the round). Organic flow continues — no bursts.
+5. **Lock + final injection** — at `T − finalInjectionLeadMs` the engine sets `tt:battle:lock:<id>`, publishes
+   `engine:events:battle.locked`, re-reads the exposure and executes the plan in ≤ `finalInjectionMaxSlices`
+   whale slices (≤ `finalInjectionMaxUsd`): *Lightning Dilution* (bisection on the winning side until real
+   winners = net real loser pool, plus `dilutionSafetyMarginPct`) or *Ghost Town* (one-sided real users:
+   inject on the opposite side by `ghostTownMarginPct`). Orders after the lock are rejected with
+   `ROUND_LOCKED`; the settlement grace key keeps the engine from settling during the injection.
+6. **Settlement** — net positions per user; `R = V_rl × (1 − fee)`; `Pot = R + V_sl`; simulator profit is capped at
+   its own losing volume, surplus goes to real winners; company = commission (+ the unpaid pool in ghost town).
+   Invariants are written to `npc_round_audit.settlement`.
+
+`engine.houseMaxRealLoserPoolRule` keeps (ON) or removes (OFF) the legacy "smaller real pot wins" rule.
+
+## Settings
+
+One JSON document, `system_settings.npc_organic_settings` (versioned, `updatedBy`), described by
+`ORGANIC_FIELD_SPECS` in `packages/shared/src/npc-organic/settings.ts`. Every field carries a label, help text,
+range and `applies` (`live` / `next_round` / `settlement`). The admin page renders the form from
+`GET /admin/npc/organic/schema`, so adding a setting is one spec entry plus its use in the engine.
+
+Propagation: DB → Redis key `ticktrade:npc:organic:settings` → pub/sub push (applied within a heartbeat) →
+20 s poll fallback → DB fallback on boot. The engine heartbeat (`ticktrade:npc:organic:engine_status`) shows
+which version it applied; the admin status bar compares it with the saved version.
+
+Legacy tabs still relevant in organic mode: **Rotation & Limits** (eligibility, cooldowns). *Volume Distribution*,
+*Pool Balance* and *NPC Behavior* only affect the legacy engine.
+
+## Admin endpoints (`npcSimulator.view` / `npcSimulator.edit`)
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| GET | `/admin/npc/organic/schema` | groups, field specs, defaults |
+| GET | `/admin/npc/organic/settings` | current document, mode, engine status |
+| PUT | `/admin/npc/organic/settings` | `{ values }` full or partial; strict validation, one `path: message` per error |
+| POST | `/admin/npc/organic/settings/reset` | directive defaults (mode kept) |
+| PUT | `/admin/npc/organic/mode` | `{ mode: 'organic' | 'legacy' }` |
+| GET | `/admin/npc/organic/status` | mode, saved version, engine heartbeat |
+| GET | `/admin/npc/organic/live` | live round telemetry (1 s) |
+| GET | `/admin/npc/organic/rounds[?limit]` · `/rounds/:battleId` | audit rows |
+
+## Frontend
+
+`battleLocked` (WS) → buttons show **LOCKED** and are disabled until the next round; the snapshot carries
+`locked` and `trader_count`. Server rejections (`ROUND_LOCKED`, `BATTLE_FROZEN`, `ORDER_FREEZE`,
+`LAST_SECOND_SNIPE_LOCK`, throttling, insufficient balance) now show a toast instead of being dropped.
+
+## Deploying
+
+1. `pnpm --filter @ticktrade/shared prisma:migrate:deploy` (adds `npc_round_audit`).
+2. Build shared → api / engine / npc-worker / settlement-worker as usual.
+3. No new environment variables. Optional: `NPC_ORGANIC_SETTINGS_POLL_MS` (default 20000).
+4. The engine starts in `organic` mode with the directive defaults; set the mode to `legacy` from the admin
+   page to fall back at any time.
+
+## Tests
+
+`packages/shared/src/npc-organic/*.spec.ts` (settings validation/coercion, plan maths, directive settlement and
+final-injection properties) and `apps/engine/src/npc-organic/organic-npc-engine.spec.ts` (round lifecycle with a
+fake clock: trickle-in, arrivals, lock at T − lead, final injection, real-trade boost, settings push).
